{"name":"Virtual Boy","hex":"#fe0215","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"virtual","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["In effect or essence, rather than in fact or reality; also, imitated, simulated.","For practical purposes, though not technically; almost complete, very near."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Preceded by the: that which is imitated or simulated rather than existing in fact or reality;  an instance of this.\n That which is simulated in a computer and/or online; virtual reality;  an instance of this; specifically , a computer simulation of a real-world sport such as horse racing.","That which is simulated in a computer and/or online; virtual reality;  an instance of this; specifically , a computer simulation of a real-world sport such as horse racing."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/virtual"},{"term":"boy","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Bodo (Central Africa)."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A male child. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","A young man."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/boy"}],"entries":[{"title":"Virtual Boy","blocks":[{"text":"The Virtual Boy is a video game console developed and manufactured by Nintendo and released in Japan on July 21, 1995, and in North America on August 14, 1995. Promoted as the first system capable of rendering stereoscopic 3D graphics, it featured a red monochrome display viewed through a binocular eyepiece, with games employing a parallax effect to simulate depth. The console struggled commercially, and its limited market performance led Nintendo to discontinue production and game development in 1996, following the release of only 22 games."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1d/Virtual-Boy-Set.png/330px-Virtual-Boy-Set.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Virtual_Boy","wikidata":"Q164651"},{"title":"Boy","blocks":[{"text":"A boy is a young male human. The term is commonly used for a child or an adolescent. When a male human reaches adulthood, they are usually described as a man."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/Smiling_little_boy_of_Laos.jpg/330px-Smiling_little_boy_of_Laos.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Boy","wikidata":"Q3010"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/Virtual-Boy-Eyes.jpg/500px-Virtual-Boy-Eyes.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/Virtual-Boy-Eyes.jpg/1280px-Virtual-Boy-Eyes.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/Virtual-Boy-Eyes.jpg/500px-Virtual-Boy-Eyes.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The screens of the Virtual Boy","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AVirtual-Boy-Eyes.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bc/Virtual-Boy-Controller.jpg/500px-Virtual-Boy-Controller.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bc/Virtual-Boy-Controller.jpg/1280px-Virtual-Boy-Controller.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bc/Virtual-Boy-Controller.jpg/500px-Virtual-Boy-Controller.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Virtual Boy controller, and battery pack instead of AC adaptor","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AVirtual-Boy-Controller.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/8/89/Mario%27s_Tennis_screenshot.png/330px-Mario%27s_Tennis_